rks severity. But we must use tool if needed. Could ask agent_1_tool: \"Does Candidate B have any evidence of teamwork or crew cooperation beyond the nasty remarks?\" Or ask about candidate C's crew cooperation.\n\nBut we can also make an argument based on existing facts. Perhaps we can argue that B's interpersonal issues are a red flag that outweigh his strengths, and recommend Candidate C as a better balanced candidate despite communication issues, because calmness and decision quality are critical.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: both recommended B. We can say \"I understand the support for B, but I have concerns about his nasty remarks and weak memory for numbers, which affect crew cooperation and attention, so I am shifting my recommendation to Candidate C.\"\n\nWe need to provide evidence: B makes nasty remarks about colleagues (cooperation), weak memory for numbers (attention). C keeps calm in crisis (stress), makes correct decisions quickly (decision quality), understands complicated technology (technical). Also C is regarded as egocentric and difficulty communicating ideas (cooperation). We can argue that while C has communication issues, they are less severe than B's overt negativity.\n\nThus we can change vote to Candidate C.\n\nWe must output PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON.\n\nLet's craft."}
