 Let's decide.\n\nGiven the discussion, we have two arguments: B strong reliability and stress, but interpersonal issues; C strong calmness, decision, technical, but communication issues. Which is more critical? Crew cooperation is vital. B's nasty remarks are severe. C's communication difficulty and egocentric may also affect crew, but less overt hostility. Also C puts concern for others above everything, which is positive for crew. That fact is in notes: \"C puts concern for others above everything.\" That is a strong crew cooperation point. So C seems better.\n\nThus I will align with Markus and vote for Candidate C. I will reference his concern for others, calmness, decision quality, and note that his communication issues are less severe than B's nasty remarks. Also bring in D as a comparison: D has responsibility but moody and loner, which may be similar to B's issues. So C remains best.\n\nThus my public message: I agree with Markus, shift to C, provide evidence: C keeps calm in crisis, makes correct decisions quickly, excellent attention, puts concern for others above everything, while B's nasty remarks and weak memory are concerning. Also note that D's moody/loner traits are also concerning, and A's unfriendly and unhealthy habits raise reliability concerns. So C is best.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
